message.content:
I enhanced the contrast and zoomed in on each tooth region. I found no clear well-defined lesions (PAI 4–5). There are two areas of faint, poorly defined apical radiolucency, both in the lower molar region, and I graded both as PAI 3. These calls are uncertain: a panoramic image has low resolution and overlapping structures in this area, so periapical radiographs would be needed to confirm them.

- **Lower left first molar** (right side of the image), at the mesial root apex: diffuse mineral loss. This is the more convincing of the two.
- **Lower right first or second molar** (left side of the image), at the root apices: faint diffuse radiolucency. I'm less sure of this one.

